<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Mcintosh bid unconditional - Merill.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Mcintosh bid unconditional - Merill.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. financial services group Merrill Lynch and Co Inc said on Tuesday it had declared its takeover offer for Australian stockbroker McIntosh Securities Ltd free from conditions.</p>
<p>Earlier today, Merrill said it had moved to 54.22 percent control of McIntosh. Merrill is bidding A$1.40 a share, an offer unanimously recommended by the McIntosh directors.</p>
<p>The offer values the company at about A$117 million.</p>
<p>McIntosh shares closed a cent higher at A$1.37 on turnover of 3.6 million shares on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
